  "report_period": "Week 45 (1st Nov to 8th Nov 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Hokoku Marine have committed their Kamsarmax \"Energy Sunrise\" 81/2014 Tadotsu, Japan (SS 06/2029, DD 04/2027, BWTS fitted) to Greek interests at excess USD 23 mill, while the scrubber fitted sister vessel \"Martha\" 81/2014 Tadotsu, Japan (SS 09/2029, DD 08/2027, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold back in September at USD 26,2 mill. In addition, the \"Pan Energen\" 81/2012 New Times, China (SS 03/2027, DD 03/2025, BWTS fitted) from Pan Ocean was committed to Turkish interests at USD 16,4 mill. Remind you that the one-year-younger \"AM Hamburg\" & \"AM Quebec\" 81/2013 New Times, China (SS 01/2028, DD 02/2026 & SS 02/2028, DD 05/2026, BWTS fitted) were sold in September at low USD 18 mill each. The Panamax \"Asia Graeca\" 73/2004 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 09/2029, DD 09/2027, BWTS fitted) of Angelakos Hellas was committed to Indonesian interests at region USD 11 mill. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the \"Scorpio WQ\" 76/2004 Sasebo, Japan (SS 02/2029, DD 07/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 10,6 mill. On the Ultramax sector, the \"Ey Haydn\" 63/2015 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to Chinese interests at region USD 32,5 mill. Remind you that back in July, the \"Swansea\" 63/2015 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 25,5 mill. Moreover, Seacon committed their \"Seacon Fuzhou\" 63/2019 Nantong, China (SS 05/2029, DD 04/2027, BWTS fitted) to clients of Shenyuan Leasing at USD 31,8 mill, while the sister vessel \"Seacon Athens\" 63/2019 Nantong, China (SS 07/2029, DD 07/2027, BWTS fitted) was sold back in August at USD 32,1 mill.",
    "tankers": "Japanese owners committed their VLCC \"Taiga\" 311/2007 Mitsui, Japan (SS 03/2027, DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) at region USD 44,5 mill. For reference, the two-years-older \"Sake\" 300/2005 IHI, Japan (SS 03/2029, DD 09/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold back in September at USD 41,75 mill. The MR2 \"Jag Padma\" 48/2005 Iwagi, Japan (SS 08/2028, DD 08/2026, BWTS fitted) of Great Eastern Shipping was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 17 mill. Remind you that the \"Daytona\" 47/2005 Onomichi, Japan (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in July at USD 17,8 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 11,000/13,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 9,000/12,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via US Gulf were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into China were reported at the level of usd 18,000/19,000 pd. South American trips into Mediterranean via Red Sea were fixed around usd 17,000/18,000 pd. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 16.900 pd for 9/12 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 9,000/11,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Indian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into East Coast India were fixed around usd 12,000/15,000 pd. South African trips into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 160K/180K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 13,000/16,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via Baltic were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via Black Sea into West Africa were reported at the level of usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Trips from US East Coast into Continent were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. South American trips into West or South Africa were reported at the level of usd 14,000/17,000 pd. A large Handysize was reported fixed in the usd 13,750 pd for 4/6 months employment basis delivery East Africa."
    }
  },
